{%- liquid
  assign sort_qs = ''
  if collection.sort_by != blank
    assign sort_qs = '?sort_by=' | append: collection.sort_by
  endif

  comment
    A tag-filtered route renders the underlying collection, so /collections/all/2014-subaru-legacy
    took its heading and breadcrumb from /collections/all — "Products" — while the browser title
    already said the vehicle. The homepage picker and vehicle-aware search both land shoppers
    here now, so the page has to name what it is showing. current_tags carries the tags the
    route filtered on, in the order Shopify matched them.
  endcomment
  assign heading = collection.title
  if current_tags.size > 0
    assign tag_names = current_tags | join: ' + '
    if collection.handle == 'all'
      assign heading = tag_names | append: ' Used Parts'
    else
      assign heading = tag_names | append: ' — ' | append: collection.title
    endif
  endif
-%}
{%- paginate collection.products by section.settings.per_page -%}
  <div class="page-width">
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="{{ routes.root_url }}">Home</a><span>/</span>
      {%- if current_tags.size > 0 -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          /collections/all is Shopify's virtual catalogue route and has no sort order of its
          own to set — it opens A-Z, which for a one-of-one salvage catalogue puts the oldest
          listings first. The site's own "Shop All Parts" link avoids it by pointing at the
          newest-first collection; this crumb, which the vehicle filters land on, carries the
          sort explicitly so dropping a filter does not drop the shopper into 1965.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- assign crumb_qs = sort_qs -%}
        {%- if collection.handle == 'all' and sort_qs == blank -%}
          {%- assign crumb_qs = '?sort_by=created-descending' -%}
        {%- endif -%}
        <a href="{{ collection.url }}{{ crumb_qs }}">{{ collection.title }}</a><span>/</span>
        <span class="muted">{{ current_tags | join: ' + ' }}</span>
      {%- else -%}
        <span class="muted">{{ collection.title }}</span>
      {%- endif -%}
    </nav>

    <div class="section-head">
      <h1 class="h1">{{ heading }}</h1>
      {%- if collection.description != blank -%}
        <div class="rte lede">{{ collection.description }}</div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    <div class="collection-layout">
      {%- comment -%} ------------------------------------------- facets {%- endcomment -%}
      <aside class="facets">
        {%- comment -%}
          Vehicle and part type always render: Shopify supplies Availability and Price
          on a real collection but nothing that narrows the yard to one truck, and on
          /collections/all it supplies no filters at all. The tag sidebar sits outside
          the filter form so its selects never trip that form's auto-submit.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {% render 'facets-tags' %}

        {%- if collection.filters.size > 0 -%}
        <form data-facet-form method="get">
          {%- if collection.sort_by != blank -%}
            <input type="hidden" name="sort_by" value="{{ collection.sort_by }}">
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- comment -%}
            Selecting a checkbox submits this form, which is a change of context the
            shopper has to be told about beforehand (WCAG 3.2.2) — hence the note. The
            <noscript> button below is the functional half: without it, and with JS off,
            a checkbox toggles visibly and does nothing at all, because the only submit
            control in this form belongs to the price fieldset.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <p class="small muted" style="margin:0 0 10px;">Filters apply as you select them.</p>

          {%- for filter in collection.filters -%}
            <details class="facets__group" {% if forloop.index < 4 %}open{% endif %}>
              <summary>{{ filter.label }}</summary>

              {%- case filter.type -%}
                {%- when 'list' -%}
                  <div class="facets__list">
                    {%- for value in filter.values -%}
                      <label class="facets__item">
                        <input type="checkbox" name="{{ value.param_name }}" value="{{ value.value }}"
                               {% if value.active %}checked{% endif %}
                               {% if value.count == 0 and value.active == false %}disabled{% endif %}>
                        <span>{{ value.label }}</span>
                        <em>{{ value.count }}</em>
                      </label>
                    {%- endfor -%}
                  </div>

                {%- when 'price_range' -%}
                  <div class="cluster" style="margin-top:12px;">
                    <label class="field" style="flex:1;margin:0;">
                      <span>Min</span>
                      <input type="number" name="{{ filter.min_value.param_name }}" inputmode="numeric"
                             value="{{ filter.min_value.value | money_without_currency | replace: ',', '' }}"
                             placeholder="0">
                    </label>
                    <label class="field" style="flex:1;margin:0;">
                      <span>Max</span>
                      <input type="number" name="{{ filter.max_value.param_name }}" inputmode="numeric"
                             value="{{ filter.max_value.value | money_without_currency | replace: ',', '' }}"
                             placeholder="{{ filter.range_max | money_without_currency | replace: ',', '' }}">
                    </label>
                  </div>
                  <button type="submit" class="btn btn--sm btn--outline" style="margin-top:10px;">Apply price</button>
              {%- endcase -%}
            </details>
          {%- endfor -%}

          <noscript>
            <p class="small muted" style="margin:10px 0 0;">
              JavaScript is off, so choose your filters and then apply them.
            </p>
            <button type="submit" class="btn btn--sm btn--outline" style="margin-top:8px;">
              Apply filters
            </button>
          </noscript>
        </form>
        {%- endif -%}

        <p class="small muted facets__help">
          Can't find it? Call the yard at
          <a class="link" href="tel:{{ settings.phone | remove: '-' | remove: ' ' }}">{{ settings.phone }}</a>
          — not everything on the lot is listed yet.
        </p>
      </aside>

      {%- comment -%} ------------------------------------------ results {%- endcomment -%}
      <div>
        {%- if current_tags.size > 0 -%}
          <div class="active-filters">
            {%- for t in current_tags -%}
              {%- liquid
                assign rest = ''
                for other in current_tags
                  unless other == t
                    assign oh = other | handleize
                    if rest == ''
                      assign rest = '/' | append: oh
                    else
                      assign rest = rest | append: '+' | append: oh
                    endif
                  endunless
                endfor
              -%}
              <span class="chip">
                {{ t }}
                <a href="{{ collection.url }}{{ rest }}{{ sort_qs }}"
                   aria-label="Remove filter: {{ t | escape }}">&times;</a>
              </span>
            {%- endfor -%}
            <a class="link small" href="{{ collection.url }}{{ sort_qs }}">Clear all</a>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        <div class="toolbar">
          <span class="toolbar__count">
            {{ collection.products_count }} part{% if collection.products_count != 1 %}s{% endif %}
          </span>
          <div class="push">
            <label class="visually-hidden" for="SortBy">Sort by</label>
            <select id="SortBy" class="select" data-sort>
              {%- assign current = collection.sort_by | default: collection.default_sort_by -%}
              {%- for option in collection.sort_options -%}
                <option value="{{ option.value }}" {% if option.value == current %}selected{% endif %}>
                  {{ option.name }}
                </option>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </select>
          </div>
        </div>

        {%- if collection.products.size > 0 -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            The card titles are h3, and the page's only heading above them was the h1, so
            the outline jumped h1 -> h3. The grid is a real section of the page and simply
            had no heading of its own; this gives it one, kept out of the visual design
            because the h1 and the filters already say what the list is. (WCAG 1.3.1.)
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <h2 class="visually-hidden">Parts in this collection</h2>
          <div class="grid grid--{{ section.settings.columns }}">
            {%- for product in collection.products -%}
              {% render 'card-product', card_product: product, eager: forloop.first %}
            {%- endfor -%}
          </div>
          {% render 'pagination', paginate: paginate %}
        {%- else -%}
          <div class="empty-state">
            <h2 class="h3">Nothing here right now</h2>
            <p class="muted">The yard turns over fast. Try a different search, or call us at {{ settings.phone }} — we'll check the racks for you.</p>
            <a href="{{ routes.all_products_collection_url }}" class="btn">Browse all parts</a>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endpaginate -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Collection",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "range", "id": "per_page", "label": "Parts per page", "min": 12, "max": 48, "step": 12, "default": 24 },
    { "type": "range", "id": "columns", "label": "Columns", "min": 3, "max": 5, "step": 1, "default": 4 }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
